{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>With Laban I sojourned</b> — that is, even though I was in Laban's house, I fulfilled the 613 commandments." "<b>And afterwards until now</b> — וא\"ת if so, that you fulfilled the commandments, come and wage battle with me. <b>And afterwards until now</b> — that is, I must delay until there passes ע\"ה (70) of Babylonia and ת\"ת (400) of Egypt and ה' אלפים (5,000), and there comes the sixth millennium, which is the days of Messiah, and afterwards: \"And saviors shall go up to Mount Zion to judge Mount Esau.\" Another interpretation: גרתי — letters of תגרי, that I was with Laban, who had with me תגרי (merchants/strife), and I am a man of strife and a master of war — all this in order to frighten him." "<b>גרתי</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here, and the other: \"Woe is me, for I have sojourned\" (Genesis 27:46) in משך. Because Jacob feared Esau and called him \"my lord,\" and HaShem had already promised him \"and I will keep you wherever you go,\" this caused his sons to become sojourners among the nations."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:32.835516521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}